abla u \cdot \vec{n}+\gamma u =0~on~\partial\Omega_1, \end{align*} where $\vec{n}$ is the normal vector of $\partial\Omega_1$ and $\gamma>0$ is a constant. We regularize this problem by correspondingly minimizing the strictly convex functional:  egin{align*} \min \limits_{a \in \mathbb A} & rac12 \int_{\Omega_1} a | {
abla(U(a)-z^\delta)}|^2 + rac12\int_{\partial\Omega_1} a\gamma [U(a)-z^\delta]^2- rac12 \int_{\Omega_1} b [U(a)-z^\delta]^2\ &+ ho \| a-a^* \|^2_{L^2(\Omega)}, \end{align*} where $U(a)$ is a map for $a$ to the solution of the Robin-boundary problem, $ho > 0$ is the regularization parameter and $a^*$ is a priori estimate of $a$. We prove that the functional attain a unique global minimizer on the admissible set. Further, we give very simple source condition without the smallness requirement on the source function which provide the convergence rate $O(\sqrt{\delta})$ for the regularized solution.

